<article class="env-lemma" id="05Q7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05Q7">Lemma <span data-tag="05Q7">4.27.18</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Let $S$ be a right multiplicative system. If $f : X \to Y$, $f' : X' \to Y'$ are two morphisms of $\mathcal{C}$ and if </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Q(X) \ar[d]_{Q(f)} \ar[r]_ a &  Q(X') \ar[d]^{Q(f')} \\  Q(Y) \ar[r]^ b &  Q(Y') }  \]
</div>
  <p> is a commutative diagram in $S^{-1}\mathcal{C}$, then there exist a morphism $f'' : X'' \to Y''$ in $\mathcal{C}$ and a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[d]_ f &  X'' \ar[l]^ s \ar[d]^{f''} \ar[r]_ g &  X' \ar[d]^{f'} \\  Y &  Y'' \ar[l]_ t \ar[r]^ h &  Y' }  \]
</div>
  <p> in $\mathcal{C}$ with $s, t \in S$ and $a = gs^{-1}$, $b = ht^{-1}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This lemma is dual to Lemma <a href="/tag/05Q3" data-tag="05Q3">4.27.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>